## Forms in this project
Forms use the `form` behavior (`import { form } from 'sygnal'`) in the component's `uses`, with a zod schema (zod is installed). It keeps the values, errors and touched fields in `state.form`, validates every change, shows a field's error once the field lost focus (every error after a submit), focuses the first invalid field on an invalid submit, and dispatches your action with the schema's output on a valid one:
```jsx
function Signup({ state, uid }) {
  const f = state.form.fields   // f.email: { name, value, error, invalid, touched, dirty }
  return (
    <form className="signup" noValidate>
      <label for={uid('email')}>Email</label>
      <input id={uid('email')} name="email" value={f.email.value} aria-invalid={f.email.invalid} aria-describedby={uid('email-error')} />
      <p id={uid('email-error')}>{f.email.error}</p>
      <button type="submit" disabled={state.form.submitting}>Sign up</button>
    </form>
  )
}
Signup.uses = { form: form(signupSchema, { values: { email: '' }, submit: 'SIGN_UP' }) }
Signup.model = {
  SIGN_UP: { HTTP: (state, values) => ({ url: '/api/signup', method: 'POST', json: values, ok: 'form.DONE', error: 'form.ERRORS' }) },
}
// main.js: run(App, { HTTP: makeFetchDriver() })
```
- Fields inside the form element are matched by `name`; they need no intent. Field arrays: rows with an `id` in `values`, named `items.<id>.field`, rendered with a Collection (`from={{ get: (s) => s.form.values.items }}`, pass `fields={f}` down), added and removed with the actions `form.ADD` `{ field, value }` and `form.REMOVE` `{ field, id }`.
- `form.ERRORS` puts server errors on their fields (a reply body `{ errors: { name: message } }` or `{ errors: [{ path, message }] }`), shows them at once and focuses the first; `form.DONE` ends the submit. A host model entry with the same name as a form action runs after the form's.
